    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup is anchored by **James Wood** (76.28) and **Austin Riley** (73.19), who present the highest ceiling based on a combination of favorable park factors and exploitable matchups. **James Wood** draws a juicy 4.84 xERA matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, and his elite 0.426 xwOBA, paired with the order-position bump, makes him the premier start of the day. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** benefits from a massive 16% park boost and a +14% SP skill advantage against the vulnerable Trevor Rogers. **Brice Turang** (72.70) remains a must-start, as his consistent efficiency against Sugano (5.12 xERA) ensures he remains a focal point for both speed and run production, which is vital given our emphasis on the scarcest category, stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (40.88), who narrowly missed the cut. While he possesses a solid base projection, he is currently running into a buzzsaw in Tarik Skubal (2.66 xERA); the combination of the elite opposing arm and a 15% penalty for the dynamic platoon shift against the southpaw pushed him just below our threshold. We are also tracking a weather-related risk for **Edwin Arroyo**, whose bench status is safer today due to a 42% rain risk that further suppresses his already marginal 41.76 efficiency score. Elsewhere, **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.68) earns a strong start despite the 4.40 xERA matchup against Zebby Matthews, as his platoon edge and second-spot order placement maximize his fantasy output potential. We remain cautious regarding **Gabriel Moreno** (48.48), whose score is suppressed by the difficult 3.45 xERA of Carson Palmquist; we are monitoring the lineup closely to ensure he stays in the #3 slot, as any drop in order would make him a candidate for mid-day reassessment to preserve game caps.",
